        "content": "# META \u2014 Catalysts\n\n## TL;DR\n\nQ1 2026 earnings (Apr 29 AH) remain the controlling catalyst on Day 2 of the post-print re-rating window. EPS beat ($7.31 adj vs $6.79 est, +7.7%) and revenue beat ($56.31B, +33% YoY) were overshadowed by capex guidance raised to **$125\u2013145B** (from $115\u2013135B; nearly double FY2025's $72B). JPMorgan downgraded post-earnings. DAP growth slowed to +4% YoY / down >5% QoQ. No new binary until Q2 2026 earnings (expected late July). Muse Spark AI model is the lone near-term positive catalyst (source: web_research/META.json, run 20260501_142327).\n\n## Live catalysts\n\n| Event | Date | Significance |\n|---|---|---|\n| Q1 2026 post-earnings re-rating window | Apr 29 \u2013 ~May 9 | HIGH \u2014 institutions still absorbing capex shock; multiple compression ongoing |\n| Layoff restructuring (8,000 employees / 10% workforce) | May 20 start | MEDIUM \u2014 cost discipline signal; offsets some capex concern |\n| Muse Spark AI model rollout | Ongoing from Apr 8 | MEDIUM positive \u2014 4th on AI Index v4.0; losing ground to Alphabet's AI monetization |\n| Social media addiction litigation | Ongoing | HIGH NEGATIVE \u2014 CA 70% liability verdict; 10,000+ suits; $375M New Mexico award |\n| Q2 2026 earnings | ~late July 2026 | MEDIUM \u2014 no confirmed date; Q2 capex commentary is the key watch |\n\n## Recent news (as of May 1, 2026)\n\n**Capex shock (HIGH):** Full-year capex raised to $125\u2013145B \u2014 highest-ever single-year commitment. No cloud revenue stream (unlike Alphabet, MSFT, Amazon) makes the spend harder to justify near-term. Free cash flow compression expected for 2\u20133 years (source: web_research/META.json, run 20260501_142327).\n\n**JPMorgan downgrade (HIGH NEGATIVE):** Downgraded April 30 post-earnings, citing capex outweighing solid Q1 results. A small cohort of analysts also shifted to Hold. Consensus remains broadly bullish (~20 Strong Buy, 18 Buy, 4 Hold, 0 Sell; avg PT ~$837), but consensus was formed pre-capex absorption \u2014 further downgrades possible (source: web_research/META.json, run 20260501_142327).\n\n**Muse Spark (MEDIUM positive):** Proprietary LLM from Meta Superintelligence Labs; early positive usage metrics. Competitor contrast: Alphabet reported Google Cloud +63% YoY to $20B \u2014 META's AI narrative is losing ground on monetization proof (source: web_research/META.json, run 20260501_142327).\n\n**Layoffs (MEDIUM):** ~8,000 employees (10% of workforce) starting May 20; 6,000 open roles frozen. Signals cost pressure is real (source: web_research/META.json, run 20260501_142327).\n",
